#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096431 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096630 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89902023-09e6-50cd-b08a-9d3e82d826c9" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Area Bounded by a Curve as a Definite Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "e375ba82-b677-5e41-a81f-cea18470ab4a" :question/math-academy-id "e-405" :question/problem "![](images/f0/f02616ea8f44865a727bec3affe596503dbadacafb113acad6e5f755218b4ff5.png)\n\nFor the function $y = -2x^3+2$ shown above, write down an expression for the area $\\mathcal{A}$ as a definite integral." :question/worked-solution "We want to express the area $\\mathcal{A}$ between the function $f(x) = -2x^3+2$ and the $x$-axis, between $x=0$ and $x=1.$\n\nThis can be expressed as the definite integral of $f(x) = -2x^3+2$ between the lower limit $x=0$ and the upper limit $x=1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\mathcal{A} = \\int_0^1 (-2x^3+2)\\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096432 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096631 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdc82e49-5df6-5096-a8fd-e00017fb1e3a" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Definite Integral as the Limit of a Left Riemann Sum"}] :question/id #uuid "cd5b3d07-472e-50cc-b584-569feb90f927" :question/math-academy-id "e-406" :question/problem "Express $\\displaystyle \\int_1^3(4-x)\\,\\textrm{d}x$ as the limit of a left Riemann sum." :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b f(x)\\textrm{d}x = \\lim_{n\\rightarrow\\infty}\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} f(x_k)\\Delta x,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $\\Delta x = \\dfrac{b-a}{n}$ and $x_k = a + k\\Delta x.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int_1^3(4-x)\\,\\textrm{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x) = 4-x,$ the lower bound is $a=1,$ and the upper bound is $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac{3-1}{n} = \\dfrac 2 n,\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(4-x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\,Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[f(1+k\\cdot \\frac{2}{n})\\,\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[f(1+\\frac{2k}{n})\\,\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[(4-(1+\\frac{2k}{n}))\\,\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[(3-\\frac{2k}{n})\\,\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096433 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096632 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f663b0b-9b5e-512c-92bb-0ea84d5baac5" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Limit of a Left Riemann Sum as a Definite Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "f7aaebcf-0a91-510e-8f09-513774affd6b" :question/math-academy-id "e-407" :question/problem "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that $\\displaystyle \\int_{3}^b f(x)\\, \\textrm d x =\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\\left[\\left(3 + \\dfrac{5k}{n}\\right)^2\\cdot \\dfrac 5 n\\right].$" :question/worked-solution "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm d x = \\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}f\\left(x_k\\right)\\cdot \\Delta x\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Delta x = \\dfrac{b-a}{n}$ and $x_k = a + k\\Delta x.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a = 3.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $\\Delta x = \\dfrac{5}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{n} = \\dfrac{b-3}{n} \\quad \\Longrightarrow \\quad b = 8.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $x_k = 3 + \\dfrac{5k}{n}$ and $f(x_k) = x_{k}^2.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\int_{3}^{8} x^2 \\, \\textrm d x =\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\\left[\\left(3 + \\dfrac{5k}{n}\\right)^2\\cdot \\dfrac 5 n\\right].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(x)= x^2$ and $b = 8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096434 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096633 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29b136d3-69bc-51ef-a262-dbee8af377d2" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Definite Integral as the Limit of a Right Riemann Sum"}] :question/id #uuid "b21e2c30-fe7d-5f6b-ade2-7324be8d273a" :question/math-academy-id "e-408" :question/problem "Express $\\displaystyle \\int_1^2 x^2\\,\\textrm d x$ as the limit of a right Riemann sum." :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b f(x)\\,\\textrm d x = \\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\sum_{k=1}^n f(x_k)\\cdot\\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwhere $x_k = a + k\\Delta x$ and $\\Delta x =  \\dfrac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int_1^2 x^2\\,\\textrm d x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x) = x^2,$ the lower bound is $a=1$ and the upper bound is $b=2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac{2-1}{n} = \\dfrac 1 n.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}f({x}_{k})\\,Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[f(1+k\\cdot \\frac{1}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[f(1+\\frac{k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[{(1+\\frac{k}{n})}^{2}\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096630 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89902023-09e6-50cd-b08a-9d3e82d826c9" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Area Bounded by a Curve as a Definite Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3245c48f-1a4d-5b3a-9824-8d88eff85902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247883} {:answer/id #uuid "630663c5-73ef-581c-8f85-9dab63b65145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(-{x}^{2}+2x-2)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248322} {:answer/id #uuid "78f4a7cf-7d63-5517-b755-104a70761128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{-3}^{0}(-{x}^{2}+2x-2)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248484} {:answer/id #uuid "907fc2ff-2b6f-5b81-8ef6-ee353873c46f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{-3}^{0}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248707} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f6fe33-4274-5a92-8a81-3a822cd289e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{-1}^{3}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3245c48f-1a4d-5b3a-9824-8d88eff85902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247883} :answer-field/id #uuid "31720fdc-70b9-5d97-9b44-5f4fe1d54cab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "63bcbbf8-c502-5d3b-bd0e-da913f8e74d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-113868" :question/problem "![](images/14/149fd953075c1d9909e036d4935ccd4f17ad1734d86bba4a70254468cd2035d5.png)\n\nFor the function $f(x)={x}^{2}-2x+2$ shown above, what is the expression for the area $A$ as a definite integral?" :question/worked-solution "We want to express the area $A$ between the function $f(x)={x}^{2}-2x+2$ and the $x$-axis, between $x=0$ and $x=3.$\n\nThis can be expressed as the definite integral of $f(x)={x}^{2}-2x+2$ between the lower limit $x=0$ and the upper limit $x=3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536862 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096630 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89902023-09e6-50cd-b08a-9d3e82d826c9" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Area Bounded by a Curve as a Definite Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52ec8218-cb93-5d37-b283-4b9bd6f9587a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{4x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536428} {:answer/id #uuid "912ffbe2-ddaf-5ff5-8704-c4428391999f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\frac{4x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536516} {:answer/id #uuid "a0021d94-413d-51d9-9095-8420090359ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536543} {:answer/id #uuid "aa06468b-d081-5ca0-9aa0-f0eefdcf9cdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536555} {:answer/id #uuid "f16db77c-2e42-5645-bf9b-aef2827a8c45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52ec8218-cb93-5d37-b283-4b9bd6f9587a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{4x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536428} :answer-field/id #uuid "203e8af7-bb35-5d46-9aaf-dc74ebadff71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b711075-e236-581f-bbc6-a977cb1be5c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-113878" :question/problem "![](images/8b/8b242c0012bdbc048f350158333b78e9484d716aa44f28511df2d7126dd02098.png)\n\nFor the function $f(x)=\\frac{4x}{1+{x}^{2}}$ shown above, what is the expression for the area $A$ as a definite integral?" :question/worked-solution "We want to express the area $A$ between the function $f(x)=\\frac{4x}{1+{x}^{2}}$ and the $x$-axis, between $x=0$ and $x=3.$\n\nThis can be expressed as the definite integral of $f(x)=\\frac{4x}{1+{x}^{2}}$ between the lower limit $x=0$ and the upper limit $x=3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{4x}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250129 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096631 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdc82e49-5df6-5096-a8fd-e00017fb1e3a" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Definite Integral as the Limit of a Left Riemann Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "054d43cb-d637-5acf-ba8c-e957170e28fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{4i/n-1}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247465} {:answer/id #uuid "0d68bdb3-37d6-567c-a5c7-49e43b6f2513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{5i/n-1}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247545} {:answer/id #uuid "bf3f8575-eadc-538e-bf1d-5ffd8ace6426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{4i/n}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249122} {:answer/id #uuid "e5731a80-e5b5-5cb0-a9bf-0807924353a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{5i/n}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249445} {:answer/id #uuid "fb85a63c-400e-593e-bc73-1a7f7b612bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{5i/n}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf3f8575-eadc-538e-bf1d-5ffd8ace6426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{4i/n}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249122} :answer-field/id #uuid "760a5e1b-de5d-5f17-aa82-85090115f907" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249872}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35148af9-fe39-53be-bd54-85b1a5b3aea3" :question/math-academy-id "q-113884" :question/problem "What is ${\\int }_{1}^{5}{e}^{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}{e}^{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)={e}^{x-1},$ the lower bound is $a=1,$ and the upper bound is $b=5.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{5-1}{n}=\\frac{4}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}{e}^{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+i\\cdot \\frac{4}{n})\\,\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(1+\\frac{4i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{1+4i/n-1}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{4i/n}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396620 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096632 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f663b0b-9b5e-512c-92bb-0ea84d5baac5" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Limit of a Left Riemann Sum as a Definite Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34cc89b8-44ed-5197-913c-4b08fc997159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f(x)={e}^{6x}$ and $b=6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396622} {:answer/id #uuid "e2308dd8-f04b-55a3-a357-4d4562b92a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f(x)={e}^{x}$ and $b=6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396623} {:answer/id #uuid "d9ab5d51-4c5d-5e5c-bd82-b3125ac54774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f(x)={e}^{6x}$ and $b=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396624} {:answer/id #uuid "68909286-13b5-56f8-91c1-b39ee0c858f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f(x)={e}^{2x}$ and $b=3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396625} {:answer/id #uuid "e106c9d7-5e46-53e8-bd3f-34d8e8d97090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f(x)={e}^{x}$ and $b=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2308dd8-f04b-55a3-a357-4d4562b92a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f(x)={e}^{x}$ and $b=6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396623} :answer-field/id #uuid "224da74b-2945-552e-a5c2-10b9f76d854e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c2081a2b-f662-517d-bd66-e0ddf60008b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-113918" :question/problem "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{6i/n}\\cdot \\frac{6}{n}].$" :question/worked-solution "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=0.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{6}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{n}=\\frac{b-0}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=6.\n$$\n\nConsequently,  ${x}_{i}=\\frac{6i}{n}$ and $f({x}_{i})={e}^{{x}_{i}}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{6}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{6i/n}\\cdot \\frac{6}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(x)={e}^{x}$ and $b=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096633 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29b136d3-69bc-51ef-a262-dbee8af377d2" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Definite Integral as the Limit of a Right Riemann Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e817c90-73b6-5e40-a4cb-de6f65f4e504" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386732} {:answer/id #uuid "eec77c43-6c27-5f35-9de9-91342da5f4f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386733} {:answer/id #uuid "f138b282-2b50-5da5-af3e-9f5891074c43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{k}{3n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386734} {:answer/id #uuid "69e645c6-0c73-5a1c-a257-403a41a6eca2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386735} {:answer/id #uuid "dce1be34-b20a-5bb8-891d-5f521a6ed79b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{3n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eec77c43-6c27-5f35-9de9-91342da5f4f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386733} :answer-field/id #uuid "1438f8f6-1b0c-5edd-937f-a796652639f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0af12d5f-0f9a-59ff-b6c2-207d86cde81b" :question/math-academy-id "q-113929" :question/problem "What is ${\\int }_{0}^{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ the lower bound is $a=0$ and the upper bound is $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-0}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[f(0+k\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[f(\\frac{3k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297288 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096630 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89902023-09e6-50cd-b08a-9d3e82d826c9" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Area Bounded by a Curve as a Definite Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15144cc0-d912-5cbb-8bbf-dcd707a34dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{-1.5}^{0.5}(-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2})^{2}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295388} {:answer/id #uuid "19d8f3ee-f891-56f8-85a4-4b9d3f48a7ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{0}^{-0.5}(-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295419} {:answer/id #uuid "2c3d2e88-7961-5153-8d27-b58d0593431b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{1.5}^{3}(-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295524} {:answer/id #uuid "a0d9b07a-4612-50bb-94a7-775c3e260dbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{1.5}^{3}(-{x}^{3}+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296122} {:answer/id #uuid "f8482f9d-8c0e-5bb3-8a19-ed6dea3549c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{-1.5}^{0.5}(-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8482f9d-8c0e-5bb3-8a19-ed6dea3549c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A={\\int }_{-1.5}^{0.5}(-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296586} :answer-field/id #uuid "70ce8762-9e32-5dac-a09d-d453cf976ae3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296866}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "faf2d8c2-4461-517c-a4d3-4a8680913bb9" :question/math-academy-id "q-30382" :question/problem "![](images/e8/e8a9dfb3ff189e96089c73ead8a3b44f04aa1684894c44203afb8884ad75c9e1.png)\n\nFor the function $f(x)=-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2$ shown above, what is the expression for the area $A$ as a definite integral?" :question/worked-solution "We want to express the area $A$ between the function $f(x)=-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2$ and the $x$-axis, between $x=-1.5$ and $x=0.5.$\n\nThis can be expressed as the definite integral of $f(x)=-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2$ between the lower limit $x=-1.5$ and the upper limit $x=0.5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-1.5}^{0.5}(-{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233800 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096632 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f663b0b-9b5e-512c-92bb-0ea84d5baac5" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Limit of a Left Riemann Sum as a Definite Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c82e992-6626-53fc-898e-a5b906c43795" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232564} {:answer/id #uuid "f2efb08c-a787-5702-bd96-8a581319d3f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2efb08c-a787-5702-bd96-8a581319d3f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536672} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4291fbb-2394-5040-b52b-01f56863c3dc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232563} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfffb626-9a15-5607-a0ea-a17a8ab45e43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfffb626-9a15-5607-a0ea-a17a8ab45e43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232566} :answer-field/id #uuid "6aceba08-75c9-55b7-9765-bf19aa269171" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232565}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "48a37973-85e7-5045-857e-c973f50df713" :question/math-academy-id "q-315828" :question/problem "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{\\,1+4k/n}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}].\n$$\n\n$\\,f(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and \n$\\,b=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=1.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{4}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{n}=\\frac{b-1}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=5.\n$$\n\nConsequently, ${x}_{k}=1+\\frac{4k}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})={e}^{\\,{x}_{k}}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[{e}^{\\,1+4k/n}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \n\n$$\nf(x)={e}^{x}\\,\\text{and}\\,b=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096630 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89902023-09e6-50cd-b08a-9d3e82d826c9" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Area Bounded by a Curve as a Definite Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5db1a8d2-e131-574b-b14e-ff9dd4c06979" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5db1a8d2-e131-574b-b14e-ff9dd4c06979" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232932} :answer-field/id #uuid "813dfcae-4912-5b30-82c0-98c6a6be4de8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232931} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4f88881-69c1-55f3-83ce-a53bedca22ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232934} {:answer/id #uuid "103ab8d5-f369-5cfd-9868-b7b325f3ef49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "103ab8d5-f369-5cfd-9868-b7b325f3ef49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536309} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb844357-e97e-53e4-b228-88705beffca1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232933} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2139c7c9-24ef-57ac-81c3-d86731b6b4f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/mat