001" :question/math-academy-id "q-73180" :question/problem "What is ${\\int }_{-2}^{3}-2{x}^{3}\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{3}-2{x}^{3}\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=-2{x}^{3},$ the lower bound is $a=-2$ and the upper bound is $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-(-2)}{n}=\\frac{5}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}-2{x}^{3}\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[f(-2+k\\cdot \\frac{5}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[f(-2+\\frac{5k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=1}^{n}[-2{(-2+\\frac{5k}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096633 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29b136d3-69bc-51ef-a262-dbee8af377d2" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Definite Integral as the Limit of a Right Riemann Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "638558e4-10ff-5afa-8bdf-9b786167c462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[5\\sqrt{-2+\\frac{5i}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{5}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536453} {:answer/id #uuid "8a534c45-0804-5cd0-ae1c-1bc24876ba0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[\\sqrt{5}{(-4+\\frac{3i}{n})}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536507} {:answer/id #uuid "a6839a44-5f1b-5130-ad49-d3732b17ae53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[5\\sqrt{-4+\\frac{3i}{n}}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536550} {:answer/id #uuid "b39b6574-f45a-534f-b0b8-98abbfe720be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[\\sqrt{5}{(-2+\\frac{3i}{n})}^{-2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536571} {:answer/id #uuid "c308f5cd-baeb-5d55-a3e9-11c3b9fac238" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[{(-4+\\frac{2i}{n})}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a534c45-0804-5cd0-ae1c-1bc24876ba0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[\\sqrt{5}{(-4+\\frac{3i}{n})}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536507} :answer-field/id #uuid "64a07a31-890d-5a37-87c6-b4aa072b0cdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4bc9664f-fb9e-55ce-8ee2-e0e93f2cfcb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-73181" :question/problem "What is ${\\int }_{-4}^{-1}\\sqrt{5}{x}^{-4}\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}\\sqrt{5}{x}^{-4}\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=\\sqrt{5}{x}^{-4},$ the lower bound is $a=-4$ and the upper bound is $b=-1.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{-1-(-4)}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{-1}\\sqrt{5}{x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[f(-4+i\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[f(-4+\\frac{3i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[\\sqrt{5}{(-4+\\frac{3i}{n})}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
